{
  "record": "qa/site7_null_abyss_20261002",
  "what": "Mean luma of the see-through void (the abyss as the player sees it between and beside the plates) in six native 1080p plate-edge views per mission, operation 10 before and after the lift of its `null` abyss, and the other missions as they ship.",
  "method": {
    "capture": "tools/capture_abyss_pairs.gd: the six cameras of tools/environment/capture_site7_plate_edges.gd (S<N>_R01, R05, O02, C03, C05, C06; zoom 1.22; shader TIME frozen to 1.0; actors, HUD and cover hidden), each shot twice, as shipped and with every plate hidden (the abyss alone). The backdrop camera_center is pinned to the capture camera (the stage is not processed while capturing).",
    "void": "pixels where the shipped frame equals the abyss-only frame within 3/255 on every channel: the plate is see-through there (void_stats.py)",
    "luma": "Rec. 601 (0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B) of the drawn code values scaled to 0..1",
    "mean_void_luma": "mean over the six views of each view's mean luma",
    "window": "windowed Godot 4.7.1, 1920x1080, gl_compatibility, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (headless does not draw shaders)",
    "before": "a temporary restore of the three files HEAD (e97fb6ac) shipped: site7_mood.json, site7_void_masks.json, site7_abyss_backdrop.gd; the working-tree versions were put back and hash-checked afterwards",
    "determinism": "two runs of the final state are bit-identical (12 of 12 frames); the \"before\" frames are one run"
  },
